{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-021",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 21,
  "title": "Proverbs 21",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 21",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 21,
  "sortOrder": 20021,
  "verseCount": 31,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The king’s heart is in the hand of the LORD, as the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "To do justice and judgment is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "An high look, and a proud heart, and the plowing of the wicked, is sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "The thoughts of the diligent tend only to plenteousness; but of every one that is hasty only to want.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "The getting of treasures by a lying tongue is a vanity tossed to and fro of them that seek death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The robbery of the wicked shall destroy them; because they refuse to do judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The way of man is froward and strange: but as for the pure, his work is right.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "It is better to dwell in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman in a wide house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbour findeth no favour in his eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "The righteous man wisely considereth the house of the wicked: but God overthroweth the wicked for their wickedness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "A gift in secret pacifieth anger: and a reward in the bosom strong wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "It is joy to the just to do judgment: but destruction shall be to the workers of iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall remain in the congregation of the dead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He that loveth pleasure shall be a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The wicked shall be a ransom for the righteous, and the transgressor for the upright.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "It is better to dwell in the wilderness, than with a contentious and an angry woman.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "There is treasure to be desired and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "A wise man scaleth the city of the mighty, and casteth down the strength of the confidence thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Proud and haughty scorner is his name, who dealeth in proud wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and spareth not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "The sacrifice of the wicked is abomination: how much more, when he bringeth it with a wicked mind?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth speaketh constantly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "A wicked man hardeneth his face: but as for the upright, he directeth his way.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "There is no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:21:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "The horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 21:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:21:31"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
